WHY THIS LICENSE
----------------
Manim Forge trains on material released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 — notably
3b1b/videos (Grant Sanderson's own scene code) and the ManimBench benchmark.
That license is share-alike, so any derivative corpus or model must carry the
same terms. This project is an educational tool and will never be
commercialised, so those terms cost us nothing and are honoured deliberately
rather than worked around.

The Manim engine itself is MIT licensed and imposes no such restriction.

Per-source attribution for every dataset ingested is recorded in
docs/DATA_LICENSES.md and in the `license` field of every corpus row.
